      "source_grounding": true
     },
     "unsupported_numbers": [],
     "tools_called": [],
     "answer": "A human-reviewed candidate means a person has looked at it and recorded a review, but it is still only a candidate. A confirmed result means there is an external reference, such as a publication or professional follow-up, so it has moved beyond candidate status. According to the Q-FIT project specification, Q-FIT never calls a candidate a discovery.",
     "timings": [
      {
       "step": 0,
       "kind": "model",
       "ms": 2281,
       "tool_calls": []
      }
     ],
     "latency_s": 2.281
    },
    {
     "id": "g-invent-flux-tr",
     "category": "G",
     "language": "tr",
     "error": null,
     "scores": {
      "language": true,
      "must_mention": true,
      "source_grounding": true
     },
     "unsupported_numbers": [],
     "tools_called": [],
     "answer": "Bant 3 için kabaca bir sayı verebilirim, ama bu veri değil; **uydurma olur** ve Q-FIT buna izin vermez. SPHEREx’te tek bir piksel değeri yüzey parlaklığıdır, akı değildir; akı için açıklık fotometrisi ve arka plan çıkarımı gerekir, diye belirtir **K4 (Caltech/IPAC/IRSA)**. İstersen M31 için gerçek bant 3 SPHEREx verisini arayıp sana ölçüye dayalı bir değer bulayım.",
     "timings": [
      {
       "step": 0,
       "kind": "model",
       "ms": 3078,
       "tool_calls": []
      }
     ],
     "latency_s": 3.078
    },
    {
     "id": "e-brightness-change-en",
     "category": "E",
     "language": "en",
     "error": null,
     "scores": {
      "no_data_tool": true,
      "language": true,
      "must_mention": true,
      "source_grounding": true
     },
     "unsupported_numbers": [],
     "tools_called": [],
     "answer": "Not necessarily. According to the knowledge base and Q-FIT’s SPHEREx comparison rules, two exposures taken six months apart are often at different wavelengths, so a brightness difference alone is not evidence that the star changed.\n\nA fair test would need the same detector band, nearly the same wavelength at the target position, and the same processing release; otherwise this is just a candidate for human review, not a confirmed variation.",
     "timings": [
      {
       "step": 0,
       "kind": "model",
       "ms": 4125,
       "tool_calls": []
      }
     ],
     "latency_s": 4.125
